TITLE: DG-1A-AR-H71 — Many-Cell Role Ecology / Local Work-Demand Proportion Audit
DATE: 2026-09-19
STATUS: SYNTHETIC / MEASURED_SANDBOX POSITIVE LOCAL-DEMAND ROLE-ECOLOGY RESULT + ROLE-CHURN/LEASE TRADEOFF
TRACK: DG-1A / ADAPTIVE-RULE RESEARCH
BRANCH: dg1a-ar
PARENT: dg1a-arh70-emergent-complementary-role-differentiation-audit.ice

PURPOSE
H70 showed that two initially symmetric regions can break symmetry and adopt complementary roles without a global role assignment.

H71 scales that question to a many-cell tissue.

The goal is NOT:

maintain a predefined role histogram.

The goal is:

let role population follow
the current spatial work ecology.

QUESTION
Can a many-cell tissue adjust role proportions using only:

LOCAL UNMET-WORK FIELDS

+

LOCAL DIFFERENTIATION PRESSURE

+

BOUNDED ROLE PERSISTENCE

without:
- global role counts;
- target percentages;
- centralized workforce allocation?

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- prove a production role-allocation law;
- freeze two roles;
- freeze a 10-step role lease;
- discover task transformations themselves;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

EVIDENCE
SYNTHETIC
MEASURED_SANDBOX

EXTERNAL-INSPIRATION CONTEXT
Flexible task allocation in social insects can arise from local work demand and response thresholds rather than central assignment.

Developmental lateral inhibition provides a separate local mechanism for reducing redundant same-state differentiation.

These are inspiration only.

H71 evidence is the synthetic benchmark below.

SPATIAL TISSUE
16 x 16 cells.

Total:
256.

Two generic work types:

A
and
B.

Each cell expresses:

ROLE A

or

ROLE B.

One cell can service:
1 local work unit / step

of its current role.

WORK ARRIVALS
Work is represented as:

LOCAL UNMET-WORK FIELDS.

The fields:
- accumulate locally;
- diffuse to nearest neighbors;
- are consumed by matching role cells.

No cell receives:
the global amount of A work
or
the global number of A-role cells.

PHASES

EQUAL DEMAND

A:
0.40 / cell-step.

B:
0.40.

A-HEAVY

A:
0.65.

B:
0.25.

B-HEAVY

A:
0.20.

B:
0.70.

EQUAL AGAIN

0.40 / 0.40.

SPATIAL HOTSPOT

upper-left:
A 0.75
B 0.15.

lower-right:
A 0.15
B 0.75.

remaining quadrants:
balanced.

TOPOLOGY DAMAGE
During part of the equal-demand phase:

a central 6 x 6 patch is unavailable.

Active cells:
220.

The demand fields remain substrate-like local state.

LOCAL ROLE SIGNAL
Each cell estimates:

local unmet A work

minus

local unmet B work.

A weak lateral differentiation term operates only when:
local work difference is ambiguous.

Thus:

strong work imbalance
can override:
checkerboard-style lateral differentiation.

PRIMARY COMPARATORS

FIXED RANDOM ROLES

LATERAL DIFFERENTIATION ONLY

UNMET-WORK RESPONSE WITHOUT ROLE PERSISTENCE

UNMET-WORK + LOCAL ROLE LEASE.

NO-LEASE RESULT
Local work-demand response strongly tracks the current ecology.

Late-phase global role fractions:

EQUAL:
approximately 0.500 A-role.

A-HEAVY:
0.684 A.

B-HEAVY:
0.270 A.

EQUAL AGAIN:
0.500 A.

These are not forced target percentages.

They emerge because:
those proportions are sufficient to service the arriving work.

SERVICE
A-HEAVY arrivals:

approximately 230.4 work units / step.

served:
230.39.

B-HEAVY:

served:
230.51.

EQUAL:

served:
204.79
of approximately 204.8 arrivals.

PRIMARY LOCAL-DEMAND POSITIVE
The tissue services essentially all arriving work
without:
a global workforce histogram.

Role abundance follows:
work backlog.

USEFUL-PROPORTION RANGE
For A-heavy demand:

A arrivals:
0.65 per cell.

B:
0.25.

Any stable A-role fraction roughly between:

0.65
and
0.75

can service both demand classes at one unit / cell-step.

Observed:

approximately 0.684.

For B-heavy:

useful A fraction:
approximately 0.20..0.30.

Observed:
approximately 0.270.

Thus:
the local controller does not converge to:
one mathematically privileged histogram.

It converges to:
a functionally sufficient role ecology.

FIXED ROLE NEGATIVE
A fixed approximately 50/50 role population accumulates very large work backlog when demand composition changes.

A-heavy service:
approximately 187.3 / step.

B-heavy:
approximately 195.5.

Backlog rises by:
orders of magnitude
relative to adaptive role allocation.

Thus:

STATIC ROLE PROPORTION
IS NOT
A ROBUST DEVELOPMENTAL STRATEGY.

LATERAL-ONLY NEGATIVE
Lateral inhibition alone holds role proportion near:

50/50

and strongly reduces same-role adjacency.

But under skewed demand it does not track:
work ecology.

A-heavy service:
approximately 191.9.

B-heavy:
approximately 179.5.

Therefore:

SYMMETRY BREAKING
IS NOT
TASK ALLOCATION.

It solves:
who becomes different.

It does not solve:
how many of each role are currently useful.

ROLE-CHURN NEGATIVE
If every cell may reconsider its role continuously from instantaneous unmet-work fields:

mean role switches:
approximately 0.755
per cell-step.

This is excessive phenotype churn.

Functional throughput is high,
but the developmental state is unstable.

Thus:

LOCAL DEMAND RESPONSE
NEEDS
ROLE PERSISTENCE.

LOCAL ROLE LEASE
Exploratory mechanism:

after a role decision,
retain the phenotype for approximately:

10 steps

before ordinary reconsideration.

Current local unmet-work evidence continues accumulating during the lease.

The lease does not:
erase reversibility.

It only prevents:
instantaneous phenotype flicker.

PRIMARY LEASE RESULT
Late phase service:

EQUAL:
204.75 / 204.8 arrivals.

A-HEAVY:
230.33 / 230.4.

B-HEAVY:
approximately 231.5
while draining previously accumulated backlog
and servicing new work.

SPATIAL HOTSPOT:
approximately 217.6 / step
against approximately 217.6 mean new arrivals.

Mean role switching:

approximately 0.0806
per cell-step.

This is roughly:

9.4x lower

than unrestricted local role response.

PRIMARY PERSISTENCE POSITIVE
A bounded local role lease preserves:

almost all useful throughput

while:
dramatically reducing role churn.

This is a direct many-cell analogue of:
H44 local version lease

and
H68 implementation-mode hysteresis.

SPATIAL ROLE ECOLOGY
At the end of the spatial-hotspot phase,
using the 10-step lease working point:

UPPER-LEFT A-HEAVY QUADRANT

A-role fraction:
approximately 77.1%.

LOWER-RIGHT B-HEAVY QUADRANT

A-role fraction:
approximately 22.9%.

The remaining quadrants remain much closer to:
mixed / balanced roles.

PRIMARY SPATIAL POSITIVE
Role population can become:
locally specialized

without:
forcing the entire organism
to adopt one global role ratio.

This is important for:
heterogeneous computational tissue.

DAMAGE RESULT
During central tissue loss:

active cells:
220.

new work arrival:
approximately 176 units / step.

10-step lease service:
approximately 175.85 / step.

Thus:
local role ecology continues servicing nearly all demand
despite:
localized cell loss.

No global rebalancer is invoked.

LEASE-LENGTH TRADEOFF
Longer leases further reduce:
role-switch frequency.

But they increase:
local work backlog
and
slow spatial reallocation.

Examples:

approximately 20-step lease:

switch rate:
~0.041 per cell-step.

approximately 40-step lease:

~0.021.

However:
work backlog grows substantially
and
hotspot adaptation becomes more inertial.

Thus:

ROLE STABILITY
vs
WORK-REALLOCATION SPEED

is another explicit developmental tradeoff.

CURRENT MANY-CELL ROLE CONTROL
LOCAL UNMET WORK

+

LOCAL NEIGHBOR DIFFERENTIATION

+

CURRENT ROLE

+

ROLE LEASE / AGE

+

OPTIONAL SLOW ROLE PRIOR

->

KEEP ROLE
or
SWITCH ROLE.

No global count is necessary.

RELATION TO H70
H70:
local lateral inhibition can break symmetry.

H71:
local unmet-work fields determine:
how much of each role is useful.

The two mechanisms answer different questions:

LATERAL DIFFERENTIATION:
WHO SHOULD BE DIFFERENT FROM WHOM?

WORK ECOLOGY:
HOW MUCH OF EACH FUNCTION IS NEEDED HERE?

ROLE LEASE:
HOW FAST SHOULD PHENOTYPE CHANGE?

RELATION TO H59
H59 showed:
target-free demand can be represented as:
local diffusive fields.

H71 uses the same principle for:
WORKFORCE / ROLE DEMAND.

Thus:
task demand
and
resource demand

may share:
one generic local field mechanism.

GENERAL PRINCIPLE
DO NOT HARD-CODE:

10% relay
30% sensor
60% processor.

Instead:

LET UNMET FUNCTION
CREATE LOCAL ROLE PRESSURE.

But:

DO NOT LET
EVERY TRANSIENT BACKLOG
IMMEDIATELY REWRITE CELL PHENOTYPE.

DECISION
AR-H71 is POSITIVE WITH A ROLE-CHURN / LEASE TRADEOFF.

Supported synthetically:

- many-cell role proportions can track changing work ecology without global role counts;
- local work fields can sustain near-complete service across large demand-ratio changes;
- lateral differentiation alone is insufficient for role proportion control;
- unrestricted demand response causes excessive role churn;
- bounded local role leases reduce switching by nearly an order of magnitude while preserving throughput;
- local spatial role specialization emerges under spatially heterogeneous work;
- localized tissue loss does not require a central workforce rebalancer.

Not demonstrated:

- more than two simultaneous roles;
- rare critical role maintenance;
- role discovery from unknown transformations;
- cell division / lineage effects;
- adversarial demand fields;
- learned lease duration.

NEXT HIGH-VALUE MOVE
AR-H72 — CONTINUOUS / POLYFUNCTIONAL PHENOTYPES VS DISCRETE ROLES

H70-H71 still make role expression discrete:

A
or
B.

A more radical question:

DO CELLS NEED DISCRETE ROLES AT ALL?

A cell could allocate:

70% capacity to A
30% to B

and continuously adapt that mixture.

Potential advantages:

- less role-switch cost;
- graceful response to mixed local demand;
- rare-role preservation;
- smoother recovery after topology loss.

Potential failures:

- loss of specialization efficiency;
- every cell becomes mediocre generalist;
- no strong division of labor;
- continuous-state noise / drift.

Compare:

A.
discrete leased roles;

B.
continuous local role mixture;

C.
mixture with specialization bonus for extreme phenotypes;

D.
rare critical task;

E.
abrupt demand shift;

F.
communication partition.

Desired:

the architecture should discover whether:
discrete cell types
or
continuous metabolic phenotypes

are actually worth their cost.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

